6. NO AI TRAINING; LIMITED INFERENCE-ONLY USE

You must not use, or knowingly supply, the Material or transformations of
it as data, examples, targets, or feedback for pretraining, continued
training, fine-tuning, reinforcement learning, distillation, or other
training or parameter optimization of an AI or machine-learning model.
This applies to commercial and noncommercial training alike.

The prohibition includes preparing training corpora; translating,
tokenizing, annotating, or otherwise transforming the Material for training;
and generating synthetic examples derived from it for subsequent training.
It also covers feeding evaluation results derived from the Material back
into training or parameter optimization. Citation is not an exception.

Private, noncommercial evaluation of a fixed model is not prohibited by this
section alone, provided it does not feed into training or parameter updates.
All other conditions still apply, including the restrictions on sharing
datasets and excerpts. Merely comparing fixed models does not itself count
as training. Learning about algorithms or independently implementing
unprotected ideas remains subject to Section 8.

For otherwise permitted private study, you may use a local inference-only
tool. You may also submit only the portions reasonably necessary to a
private session with a hosted inference service, but only where its
applicable terms and settings prohibit using the submitted Material and
outputs derived from it for training, prohibit public sharing, and limit
the provider's rights to processing, securing, and retaining the session
as reasonably necessary to provide the service. You must not grant broader
independent reuse or sublicensing rights in the Material.

This is a narrow exception to Section 3 for service processing, not permission
to create a shared retrieval corpus, upload the whole repository, or grant
a service a training license. If you cannot establish these conditions,
use a local tool or obtain written permission. Outputs that reproduce or
adapt the Material remain subject to the applicable restrictions.

